he service here is always excellent.  Needed to get a quick meal for my wife and I today, and couldn't have had a better experience overall.  What a local gem.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2021-03-25 02:29:58\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":3.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"Food was not as cheap as I anticipated it would be. 14 dollars for a burrito and bottle of water. The burrito was pretty good, but I found the chicken to be a bit dry. The salsa has decent flavor, but was not spicy. Overall decent food\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2020-09-11 02:31:03\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":4.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"This El Sitio location is near home, but I've seldom been there. Now they serve only to-go, so calling your order in is a good option - ready in ten minutes. Yesterday we had 2 burritos - Adobado and pork chile verde. Both were huge and very good, for $9.50 each. You have a choice of salsas to go with. We had the verde (fairly mind). The red sauce will make you sweat, which is what you want sometimes, with a cold beer.\\\"}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"CA\\\"}\", \"original_answer\": \"El Sitio is a Mexican restaurant located at 7398 Calle Real, Goleta, CA, open from 8:00 to 20:30, Monday to Saturday. The establishment has a casual ambience and is suitable for groups. It offers take-out options but does not provide outdoor seating, Wi-Fi, or music. Street and lot parking are available, but there is no garage, valet service, or parking validation. It has an overall business rating of 4 stars. Customer reviews highlight the excellent service, good food, and quick preparation time. However, some customers have noted that the pricing might be higher than expected, with one customer mentioning a $14 charge for a burrito and bottle of water. The restaurant's burritos are praised for their size and quality, although one customer found the chicken a bit dry. The salsa is noted to have a decent flavor, but it is not particularly spicy.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in_original_response\